            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="1032" n="912" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg912"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2649: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-23T17:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 23—8:06
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>140. Your number 87, August 11, 5 p.m., received August 15th and your number 91,
                    August 15, 5 p.m., under date of August 16. I formally communicated memorandum
                    to Foreign Office and asked for reply and today I am in receipt of reply under
                    date of August 22nd in exact terms of memorandum transmitted in my number 135,
                    August 9, 1 p.m. I am sending a copy of my note and reply by mail.<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d738-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
